// texteditor_opendoc_setup.cla: gated-UI-scenario-ONLY companion, compiled
// TOGETHER with examples/texteditor.cla (test-consolidation Task 5, audit
// rows N11/R6 MERGE->N14/[texteditor]) -- never part of the acceptance app
// itself. Its sole job is to self-write two small real fixture files,
// entirely within the same boot texteditor.events then `launchdoc`s them
// in, so `App.openDocument`'s real `file.readText` (examples/
// texteditor.cla's `openPath`) SUCCEEDS instead of falling into its
// couldn't-open `alert()` branch.
//
// That success matters mechanically, not just semantically: alert() text
// is NOT part of the RT_MAC_TEST trace/snap vocabulary (rt_mac.c's
// RT_MAC_TEST rt_alert / this port's nat_UiTestEmit both append straight
// into the SAME capture stream parseUIOutput reads, as a bare line with
// no "T " prefix), so an unhandled alert() firing mid-script would hit
// parseUIOutput's "unexpected capture line" fatal. testdata/ui/
// texteditor_bigfile_setup.cla (retired, test-consolidation Task 4) hit
// this exact alert() deliberately, on purpose, and needed a bespoke
// capture-stripping helper to cope; this fixture keeps both launchdoc'd
// reads inside the textview's ordinary size range precisely to avoid
// needing that machinery here.
//
// Hooked to `on App.launch` rather than `App.startEmpty`: per Ch7's
// Launch Order, `launch` always fires first, but `startEmpty` and
// `openDocument` are mutually exclusive -- and this scenario's whole
// point is for BOTH launchdoc'd paths to dispatch openDocument, so the
// write must happen on the one event that still runs on that branch.
//
// The second path ("My Notes.txt") deliberately contains a space --
// the retired testdata/ui/opendoc.cla scenario's own proof that
// rt_ui_launch's launchdoc pre-scan reads the REST OF THE LINE (not a
// whitespace-split token) for a doc path; this file preserves that same
// shape for texteditor.events' own launchdoc lines.
on App.launch {
    var t1: text
    var t2: text

    t1.append("Quarterly report draft.")
    file.writeText("Report.txt", t1)

    t2.append("Meeting notes for today.")
    file.writeText("My Notes.txt", t2)
}
